{
  "reason": "Select only model_design because temporal filtering belongs to the model and all host components are frozen. The ungated depthwise model already achieves HR@10=0.625, matching the gating attempt; limited access to adjacent transitions within higher-dilation filters is a plausible hypothesis, not an established cause. Historical factorization success supports retaining depthwise filtering, while the failed shorter-dilation experiment favors adding local access without reducing the existing receptive field.",
  "module": ["model_design"],
  "plan": {
    "data_processing_and_feature_engineering": null,
    "model_design": "In NextItNetBlock.__init__, add self.local_conv1 only when dilation > 1 as an nn.Conv1d with hidden_units input/output channels, the existing kernel_size, dilation=1, groups=hidden_units, padding=0, and bias=False. Preserve the _causal_conv signature but compute pad = (self.kernel_size - 1) * conv.dilation[0]; in forward, apply self.conv1 and self.local_conv1 to the same normalized, masked, transposed y and average their outputs with factor 0.5 before self.mix1, retaining the existing path for dilation-1 blocks. This adds immediate-transition filtering while preserving the [1,2,4,8,1,2,4,8] schedule and 121-position maximum receptive field; keep conv2, mix2, activations, residual connections, normalization, dropout, masks, embeddings, initialization, and candidate scoring unchanged, without introducing gating, dense temporal convolutions, or depth aggregation. Preserve all existing variable names and constructor, forward, encode_sequence, score_candidates, and helper interfaces, exactly the three permitted imports and two classes with methods only, and MAXLEN=128, HIDDEN_UNITS=64, NUM_BLOCKS=8, KERNEL_SIZE=3, DROPOUT_RATE=0.2, LR=0.001, WEIGHT_DECAY=0.0, BATCH_SIZE=128. Allocate one of the 44 total candidate slots to this single architectural change and let the unchanged seed-2024 host compare validation HR@10 against 0.625, interpreting any gain cautiously given 200 validation users and leaving all training, evaluation, checkpointing, and candidate-score generation to the host.",
    "training_evaluation": null
  }
}
